@@ -1 +1 @@
-Owner skill: `skill://rust-conventions`. Dev-only test fixture: `conflict_repo(files)` builds a real temp repo (user and system git config, XDG attributes/ignore files and env-passed config isolated; `GIT_EDITOR=:` and no `GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR`, so a `--continue` never waits for an editor) whose `git merge` stops with the scripted conflicts (regular files, symlinks, submodule gitlinks via `FileKind`); `conflict_repo_with(files, setup)` also sets repo config (in force for the merge too) and a `.gitattributes` committed with base. Every builder starts from one `empty_repo()`, whose own config holds `REPOSITORY_CONFIG` (`core.autocrlf=false`, the committer and `commit.gpgsign=false`), so git run outside the sandbox (`yamt_gitio::Repo`'s Continue) can commit there too; the sandboxed `git` passes the same values as `-c`. `operation_repo(run, files)` (`src/operation.rs`) = `ready_repo(run, files)` (everything committed, nothing run; what an abort must give back) then `start(run, root)`, for any `Run`: `Merge`, `SquashMerge` (of the three steps), `Rebase`, `RebaseApply`, `RebaseInteractive` (a `reword` left at step 3), `RebaseSquash` (step 2 a `squash` into step 1), `RebaseMerges` (`git rebase -r` re-doing the merge of `remote` into `local`: `MERGE_HEAD` and `REBASE_HEAD`, one stop), `CherryPick`, `CherryPickRange`, `Revert`, `RevertRange`, `Am` (`git am -3`, the mailbox on stdin), `StashPop`; a run that does not stop (also `conflict_repo_with`'s merge) is `Error::DidNotStop { run }`. In every run stage 2 is `local`, stage 3 `remote`, stage 1 `base`. Sequences (the four other rebases, the two ranges, `Am`) have three steps: step 1 conflicts in the caller's files, step 2 in `STEP_TWO_FILE` whatever step 1 was resolved to, step 3 applies cleanly; rebases replay branch `remote` onto `local`, picks and `am` apply `main..remote` on `local`, reverts undo `HEAD~4..HEAD~1` (step 1 = `HEAD~1`); step 1's message is `STEP_ONE_MESSAGE` ("step 1" with a body). `edit_stop_repo(files)` is a rebase of `remote` onto `main` stopped without a conflict at an `edit` of step 1. `rerere_repo(remembered, fresh, replay)` (`src/rerere.rs`, plan §2 #90) stops a second merge on `local` after a first merge of `remote` with `rerere.enabled`, in which each `Remembered { file, resolution }` was resolved and committed; `Replay` decides the rest: `Review`/`Stage` (`rerere.autoUpdate` false/true) undo that merge and merge `remote` again, so rerere replays each resolution; `Off` keeps the merge commit, switches `rerere.enabled` off and merges branch `later`, leaving the empty `MERGE_RR` that commit wrote (no checkout after it: a checkout drops `MERGE_RR`), so only `fresh` files conflict. Each `fresh` file conflicts only in the second merge and needs sides no remembered file has (rerere identifies a conflict by its text). `install_hook(root, name, script)` writes a hook and points `core.hooksPath` at it, over any user setting. `run_ignored_in_child(tests, configure)` reruns ignored tests of the running test binary in a child process `configure` sets up (an environment the test process cannot change for itself), `Error::ChildTestsFailed` with the child's output unless all passed. `FileKind::Symlink` exists on unix only, so a fixture element or test that scripts a link carries `#[cfg(unix)]` or fails to compile for Windows. The one source of scripted conflicts for `gitio` and `session` tests; library code, so it returns `Result` and never unwraps.
+Owner skill: `skill://rust-conventions`. Dev-only test fixture: `conflict_repo(files)` builds a real temp repo (user and system git config, XDG attributes/ignore files and env-passed config isolated; `GIT_EDITOR=:` and no `GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR`, so a `--continue` never waits for an editor) whose `git merge` stops with the scripted conflicts (regular files, symlinks, submodule gitlinks via `FileKind`); `conflict_repo_with(files, setup)` also sets repo config (in force for the merge too) and a `.gitattributes` committed with base. Every builder starts from one `empty_repo()`, whose own config holds `REPOSITORY_CONFIG` (`core.autocrlf=false`, the committer and `commit.gpgsign=false`), so git run outside the sandbox (`yamt_gitio::Repo`'s Continue) can commit there too; the sandboxed `git` passes the same values as `-c`. `operation_repo(run, files)` (`src/operation.rs`) = `ready_repo(run, files)` (everything committed, nothing run; what an abort must give back) then `start(run, root)`, for any `Run`: `Merge`, `SquashMerge` (of the three steps), `Rebase`, `RebaseApply`, `RebaseInteractive` (a `reword` left at step 3), `RebaseSquash` (step 2 a `squash` into step 1), `RebaseMerges` (`git rebase -r` re-doing the merge of `remote` into `local`: `MERGE_HEAD` and `REBASE_HEAD`, one stop), `CherryPick`, `CherryPickRange`, `Revert`, `RevertRange`, `Am` (`git am -3`, the mailbox on stdin), `StashPop`; a run that does not stop (also `conflict_repo_with`'s merge) is `Error::DidNotStop { run }`. In every run stage 2 is `local`, stage 3 `remote`, stage 1 `base`. Sequences (the four other rebases, the two ranges, `Am`) have three steps: step 1 conflicts in the caller's files, step 2 in `STEP_TWO_FILE` whatever step 1 was resolved to, step 3 applies cleanly; rebases replay branch `remote` onto `local`, picks and `am` apply `main..remote` on `local`, reverts undo `HEAD~4..HEAD~1` (step 1 = `HEAD~1`); step 1's message is `STEP_ONE_MESSAGE` ("step 1" with a body). `edit_stop_repo(files)` is a rebase of `remote` onto `main` stopped without a conflict at an `edit` of step 1. `sed_sequence_editor(scripts)` is the one way fixtures and tests build a `git -c sequence.editor=…` value: `sed -i.orig -e '<script>' …`, the backup suffix attached because BSD sed (macOS) takes the argument after a bare `-i` as the suffix. `rerere_repo(remembered, fresh, replay)` (`src/rerere.rs`, plan §2 #90) stops a second merge on `local` after a first merge of `remote` with `rerere.enabled`, in which each `Remembered { file, resolution }` was resolved and committed; `Replay` decides the rest: `Review`/`Stage` (`rerere.autoUpdate` false/true) undo that merge and merge `remote` again, so rerere replays each resolution; `Off` keeps the merge commit, switches `rerere.enabled` off and merges branch `later`, leaving the empty `MERGE_RR` that commit wrote (no checkout after it: a checkout drops `MERGE_RR`), so only `fresh` files conflict. Each `fresh` file conflicts only in the second merge and needs sides no remembered file has (rerere identifies a conflict by its text). `install_hook(root, name, script)` writes a hook and points `core.hooksPath` at it, over any user setting. `run_ignored_in_child(tests, configure)` reruns ignored tests of the running test binary in a child process `configure` sets up (an environment the test process cannot change for itself), `Error::ChildTestsFailed` with the child's output unless all passed. `FileKind::Symlink` exists on unix only, so a fixture element or test that scripts a link carries `#[cfg(unix)]` or fails to compile for Windows. The one source of scripted conflicts for `gitio` and `session` tests; library code, so it returns `Result` and never unwraps.
